class org.mockito.internal.stubbing.defaultanswers.RetrieveGenericsForDefaultAnswers {
@Nullable
  static Object returnTypeForMockWithCorrectGenerics(
      InvocationOnMock invocation, AnswerCallback answerCallback) {
    Class<?> type = invocation.getMethod().getReturnType();

    final Type returnType = invocation.getMethod().getGenericReturnType();

    Object defaultReturnValue = null;

    if (returnType instanceof TypeVariable) {
      type = findTypeFromGeneric(invocation, (TypeVariable) returnType);
      if (type != null) {
        defaultReturnValue = delegateChains(type);
      }
    }

    if (defaultReturnValue != null) {
      return defaultReturnValue;
    }

    if (type != null) {
      if (!MOCKITO_CORE.isTypeMockable(type)) {
        return null;
      }

      return answerCallback.apply(type);
    }

    return answerCallback.apply(null);
}
}
```


### Response Format:

**If the method CANNOT return null at this specific call site:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[EXPLAIN WHY THE INVOCATION MockUtil.getMockHandler(invocation.getMock()) RESULT CANNOT BE NULL.]]></reason>
  <value>NO</value>
</response>
```

**If the method CAN return null at this specific call site:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[EXPLAIN WHY THE INVOCATION MockUtil.getMockHandler(invocation.getMock()) RESULT CAN BE NULL.]]></reason>
  <value>YES</value>
</response>
```

**If you need declarations of other methods to make a determination:**
```xml
<response>
  <reason><![CDATA[Explain why you need these method declarations to make a confident decision]]></reason>
  <success>false</success>
  <methods>
    <method>methodName</method>
  </methods>
</response>
```
### Instructions for Requesting Method Declarations:
